.TH ZFSBACKUP-CONFIG 1 "October 2026" "zfsbackup" "ZFS Backup"
.SH NAME
zfsbackup\-config \- manage the zfsbackup configuration database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfsbackup\-config
.RB [ \-c
.IR DATABASE ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-reload\-wait
.IR SECONDS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B zfsbackup\-config \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zfsbackup\-config
is the only writer of the zfsbackup configuration, the host identity and
(beside the daemon's API) the trust tables.
After every committed write it asks the running
.BR zfsbackupd (1)
to reload, and waits up to \fB\-\-reload\-wait\fR seconds for the answer.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B import \fIFILE.yaml\fR
Replace the stored configuration with a YAML file (the outgoing one is backed up
next to the database).
.TP
.B export
Print the stored configuration as YAML.
.TP
.BR list " datasets|destinations"
Show the stored datasets or destinations.
.TP
.BR get ", " set ", " unset
Read, change or revert one setting by its dotted path.
.TP
.B edit
Edit the configuration, or one dataset or destination, in $EDITOR.
.TP
.B rename
Rename a dataset or a destination, with its ZFS property side effects.
.TP
.B enroll \fIDESTINATION\fR
Enroll this host with a backup server using an enrollment token.
.TP
.B identity
Show or change this host's client id; rotate its client certificate.
.TP
.B trust
Server side of enrollment: enrollment tokens and the trusted client list.
.TP
.B status
Compare the stored configuration with the one the daemon has applied.
.TP
.B check
Grade the backup health (text, JSON, Prometheus or Nagios output).
.TP
.B backup \fIDIR\fR
Back up the database and the TLS files into a new directory under DIR.
.TP
.B migrate
Bring the database schema up to the installed version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIDATABASE\fR
The configuration database.
Default: $ZFSBACKUP_CONFIG, else /var/lib/zfsbackup/config.db.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.TP
.BI \-\-reload\-wait " SECONDS"
Wait this long for the daemon to acknowledge a reload (default 3; 0 does not
wait). It goes before the command and never changes the exit status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 invalid input or refused; 2 usage error; 75 conflict or busy, retry;
78 the configuration database is unusable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/zfsbackup/config.db
The configuration database. Operators who may run this command are members of
the \fBzfsbackup\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zfsbackupd (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/zfsbackup/README.md
